@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# R50 — E2LB 0x4300 A/B fallback
+
+## Evidence from the supplied R44 log
+
+The supplied three-attempt trace shows the same sequence in each attempt:
+
+1. The sender submits `0x4300` using `DUAL_GROUP`.
+2. No `0x4301` is observed.
+3. The receiver emits DETECT markers.
+4. A new pure SYN arrives with a changed sequence/session negotiation context.
+5. The current iAP2 link is retired.
+
+This is a strong correlation, not proof that the DUAL_GROUP body caused the receiver restart. The source already exposes a user opt-in DUAL_GROUP experiment, so R50 uses a bounded A/B fallback rather than changing the protocol globally.
+
+## Runtime behavior
+
+- The user's DUAL_GROUP preference remains unchanged.
+- A fallback is recorded only for E2LB and only when all conditions hold:
+  - the selected body was `DUAL_GROUP`;
+  - the `0x4300` control frame was generated;
+  - the local stream write returned successfully;
+  - the observed receipt ended from `FRAME_GENERATED` (not `PEER_ACKED`);
+  - the link ended because the peer restarted iAP2 negotiation;
+  - no `0x4301` was received.
+- The receiver key is a SHA-256 fingerprint of the local binding plus normalized receiver capability identity. Each fingerprint has its own preference key, so separate receiver profiles do not overwrite one another. No raw Bluetooth address or receiver display name is stored in this preference.
+- On the next attempt for that fingerprint, the sender uses `SINGLE_GROUP` while leaving the user's experiment toggle on. The log explains the fallback.
+- Manually changing the experiment toggle clears all remembered per-receiver fallbacks so the user can intentionally retry DUAL_GROUP.
+- No other receiver is affected.
+
+## Diagnostic improvements
+
+`Iap2LinkChannel` now counts peer payload frames and ACK-only frames separately. `Iap2AvailabilityProgress` distinguishes:
+
+- not transmitted;
+- local write incomplete;
+- link ended;
+- transport ACK received but no `0x4301`;
+- DETECT-only activity;
+- ACK-only activity;
+- peer payload activity without `0x4301`;
+- no peer activity.
+
+A transport ACK is still not treated as CarPlay application acceptance.
+
+## Safety / non-claims
+
+- No iAP2 wire format was changed.
+- No retransmission, SYN, DETECT, or MFi behavior was changed.
+- The fallback is an evidence-driven compatibility experiment, not a verified diagnosis of the receiver's firmware.
+- A successful `SINGLE_GROUP` attempt must still be confirmed by a real `0x4301`, Wi-Fi handoff, AirPlay SETUP/RECORD, and actual video/audio/touch.
+- If `SINGLE_GROUP` also fails, the next required evidence is a new diagnostic log from R50 showing the selected shape, receipt state, local-write state, ACK-only/payload counters, and peer termination reason.
